  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SPVO &#x2013; Social Blocks</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main goal of the project is to formalise brick producers both technically and socially certified, so they will be able to supply bricks to internationally funded infrastructure projects. These constrcution companies are willing to pay more money for socially and technically certified bricks. In order to sell bricks to them, informal brick producers will have to abide by the rules of the certification process. This financial incentive is how we can diminish child labour, create safer work environments and ensure that internationally funded projects can work with ethically produced bricks..</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">There are a lot of informal brick producers in Ghana. The employees work under poor conditions, they have little training to operate the machines, the work is often done without safety gear and sometimes the employees are underage. Certification can be a tool to combat child labour and bad working conditions.There are two different forms of certification. Technical certification ensures that the bricks meet the quality and safety standards. Right now, it is an expensive process that many informal brick producers cannot afford. Social certification ensures that employees work under safe working conditions and that child labour is minimised.This project aims to combine both technical and social certification in one decentralised process. By making it decentralised, certification becomes much cheaper.When informal brick producers become both technically and socially certified, they will be able to supply bricks to internationally funded infrastructure projects. These projects are willing to pay more money for socially and technically certified bricks. In order to sell bricks to them, informal brick producers will have to abide by the rules of the certification process. This financial incentive is how we can diminish child labour, create safer work environments and ensure that internationally funded projects can work with ethically produced bricks.At the end of the project, the goal is to have set up a company that performs the certification process and the checks thereafter. When a brick producer does not meet the requirements, it will be explained what adjustments they have to make in order to pass certification. This way a positive impact can be realised that is sustainable long term.</narrative>
  </description>
